Regression-candidate confirmation (flagged by review, NEARS-2748-R1, orthogonal
to NEARS-1614 — pre-existing mobile/desktop asymmetry, NOT introduced by this
ticket's diff).

Static: pick_map_screen.dart's MOBILE-render onMapCreated block (line ~405-418)
only guards on `!widget.fromAddAddress` (this ticket removed the dead
`widget.route != RouteHelper.onBoarding` clause from it). The DESKTOP-render
block (line ~236-245) still guards `!widget.fromAddAddress && widget.route !=
'splash'` — added by NEARS-2748-R1, never ported to the mobile block. This
means on a mobile form factor, arriving at the pick-map/location-gate screen
via the NEW first-run flow (route == 'splash') DOES trigger an auto
getCurrentLocation() fetch that the desktop path skips.

Live confirmation (emulator-5558, mobile form factor, first-run flow,
permission denied): getCurrentLocation() fires immediately on
onMapCreated even though route == 'splash', producing a paired,
correctly-logged [FAIL] (not silent):

09-02 00:28:09.068 27329 27329 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=null http_status=null type=GetPositionFailure msg="location: getPosition threw (PermissionDeniedException) — falling back to default position"
09-02 00:31:08.801 28044 28044 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=null http_status=null type=GetPositionFailure msg="location: getPosition threw (PermissionDeniedException) — falling back to default position"

Reproduced identically across BOTH the fresh first-run (pid 27329) and the
relaunch (pid 28044) — the guard gap is deterministic, not flaky.

This is real, reproducible behavior — NOT a NEARS-1614 regression (pre-existing
mobile/desktop asymmetry, guard clause the ticket touched never excluded
'splash' on mobile, only excluded the now-deleted onboarding route). Filed to
regression_bugs per the QA contract; does not affect this ticket's verdict.
